# Bytes a pull request may grow the linux/amd64 release binary over its base,
# checked by `make size-growth-check` in CI. The number counts only while the
# pull request edits this file; otherwise the allowance is 16384 bytes.
# A pull request that needs more sets the bytes here and says why in a comment above them.
# #3938: the Apply confirm reads the native hook and MCP records sync
# writes (env masking, quoting, url redaction), and approvals, targets and
# builtins edits of the home config share one lock and one snapshot read.
# The preview also reads Grok and TOML hooks, keeps Vibe MCP aliases,
# and masks credentials in command arguments. No new dependency.
